[Music]  The Wall Street Journal recently  reported on the so-called Bladerunner  curse in that 1982 sci-fi cult classic  starring Harrison Ford some real-world  corporations of 1982 appear prominently  in the dark neon-lit  cityscape of a fictional 2019 director  Ridley Scott's goal was to convey a  gloomy foreboding about the triumph of  corporate power in our not-too-distant  future  the curse is that many of the companies  in the movie such as Pan Am and Bell  Telephone no longer exist or were  gobbled up it's a curse allegedly  because this is supposedly unusual but  for all of their corporate power big  corporations are often powerless when it  comes to the simple task of surviving  only 67 of the firms in the fortune 500  and 1955 were still there by 2011 the  rest were lost like tears and rain the  lesson is that if you're worried about  corporate power don't be afraid of the  market but do be afraid of companies  joining with governments to artificially  extend their lifespan what do you think  about corporate power and our dystopian  future let us know in your comments also  let us know what other topics you'd like  our scholars to cover in 60 seconds and  be sure to subscribe for more research  and videos from the American Enterprise  Institute

